    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "HippoRAG uses a <strong>large language model (LLM)</strong> to transform a corpus into a schemaless knowledge graph (KG), which serves as the artificial hippocampal index. Given a new query, HippoRAG identifies key concepts in the query and runs the <strong>Personalized PageRank (PPR) algorithm</strong> on the KG to integrate information across passages for retrieval.",
      "visualization": {
        "type": "flow-diagram",
        "description": "A flowchart showing the HippoRAG process, from offline indexing to online retrieval, with the LLM, KG, and PPR algorithm interacting to retrieve relevant passages.",
